  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Third Fiscal Consolidation and Inclusive Growth DPO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Third Fiscal Consolidation and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Financing in Cameroon is to improve the equity and efficiency in the allocation and use of health resources as well as social services including by scaling up social protection.  The series is organized around three pillars. Pillar 1 improves fiscal sustainability and public sector management by strengthening public debt management improving public procurement processes and the transparency of COVID-19 response funds. Pillar 2 enhances competitiveness by reducing entry barriers, improving regulations in strategic sectors, and incentivizing private sector investment in three strategic sectors (telecommunications, energy, and transport). Pillar 3 improves social services and scales up social protection. The reforms under this pillar aimed to improve the equity and efficiency in the allocation and use of health resources as well as social services including by scaling up social protection.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the proposed Third Fiscal Consolidation and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Financing operation are to support the Government of Cameroon&apos;s efforts to : (i) ensure fiscal sustainability and improve public-sector management, (ii) enhance competitiveness, and (iii) enhance the provision of social services and scale up social protection.</narrative>
  </description>
